    delaySeconds: 0
    decaySeconds: 0.15
  contentsAnswer: Machine fitter. Replacement spanners and sockets for the morning
    shift.
  weightAnswer: Eleven kilos. The tool case is on my job sheet.
  metalAnswer: Steel tools, almost the whole case. The handle is the only plastic
    part.
  packingAnswer: Individual slots, trays bolted down. I do not let tools bounce around.
  responseAnswer: A latch can rattle. There are no springs or moving units in the
    load.
  authorReasoning: 'Carrier: 10.8 kg is plausible, but metal about 9/100 conflicts
    with an almost entirely steel load. Clear delayed pulse further contradicts fixed
    tool trays.'
